My priority list for formal identification then runs
something like this:
 1. Any wands of wishing I am fortunate enough 
    to have acquired.
 2. At least one wand of fire or lightning, if I have
    one, or of digging in a pinch, so I have a reserve 
    of known charges for engraving Elbereth.
 3. A wand of death, if I have one.  (If I
    have two different kinds of wands that make
    the bugs on the floor stop moving, I price
    check to find out which is which, because
    wands of sleeping are not a formal ID
    priority at this point in the game.)
 4. Any scroll worth 300zm (unless I have
    already identified charging and genocide).
 5. Any ring worth 300zm (unless I already
    feel very firm).
 6. Important magic armor (e.g., if I
    want to know which cloak provides MR).
 7. A magic marker, if I have one.
 8. Additional important wands.
 9. 200zm rings (looking for slow digestion).
10. 100zm scrolls.
11. Weapons whose enchantment level I
    really want to know.

Usually by the time I read enough blessed
scrolls to get that far through the list,
one of them will ID everything I'm holding.
After reading each scroll I put away the 
stuff that just got identified and get out 
other stuff to fill my inventory slots, to 
maximize my benefit when that happens.

